guamp: shader priming replays the render server's journal of pipelines once per runtime and Turnip build (precompilation)

Every new image changes the bridge's runtime, which keys the shader cache, and Turnip's build, which keys its own: fin50
(live-20261105-204852) made 155 render pipelines in 15.5 s with "V cache hit0 miss286", the slowest 832 ms, most between 90 and
330 s while the user opened things; a boot with a warm cache makes one in about 21 ms (live-20261103-192306: 104 pipelines, 2184 ms, hit104). The library pass of
PrimeShaders.h cannot warm them: it makes each vertex function with one BGRA8 attachment and no constants, while QuartzCore draws
fixed_frag_lph_cpf with about 200 constant sets and their own blending (90 % of the journal's time).

PrimeShaders.h now reads the tail (8 MiB) of pipelines.log, the frontend's journal of every render pipeline the render server made
(both functions with every constant, the attachments with their blending, the vertex descriptor, samples, topology, depth and
stencil formats), keeps the distinct descriptors (269 in the last 8 MiB of the 20261104-160143 dump, all QuartzCore's), and makes
the most frequent first (at most 400) from QuartzCore's default.metallib, 30 s after the device opened instead of the library
pass's 90 s, each after waitForQuiet() and at background QoS like the library pass; the library pass follows at its own delay.
prime-replay-done lists the builds (buildId(): translator digest and Turnip's LC_UUID) already replayed, prime-current/prime-bad
leave out a descriptor that ended the process, NMB_PRIME_REPLAY=0 turns it off. prime.log gets "replay lines=.. unique=.. tried=..
made=.. refused=.. skipped=.. ms=.. waited=..", and each made pipeline counts in the PR row's made=. Host check: the header compiles
with clang -fsyntax-only as Objective-C++ against stand-in Foundation/Metal headers (the CI builds it for real); the journal key
extraction was replayed in Python on the 20261104-160143 journal. Applies after 0001-0003, 0009-0030 (none touches PrimeShaders.h).

